1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:01,940
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,340
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:06,010
(Episode 31)

4
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:11,580
Yes. This is Kang Da Mi,
the manager...

5
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:13,820
This is Kang Da Mi.

6
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:15,590
Yes, go ahead.

7
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,790
About the job...

8
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:19,720
I will take it.

9
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:24,660
I've actually been waiting.

10
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:27,130
This is very welcome
news to me, Ms. Kang.

11
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,900
When can you start?

12
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:32,740
I would like to start
as early as tomorrow.

13
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:35,170
Sounds good.

14
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,340
Let us start working together
tomorrow, then.

15
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:39,440
I'll hang up now.

16
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,640
Ever since you came into this house,

17
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,440
my sister's life has gone
completely down the drain.

18
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:09,910
My brother-in-law ran off
with another woman, had a kid,

19
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:12,310
and started a whole new family.
Am I wrong?

20
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:34,930
(Living Expenses
Savings: 2,640 dollars)

21
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:44,040
I worked like crazy
and saved like crazy,

22
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,340
so why am I broke?

23
00:01:48,010 --> 00:01:49,350
If I want to move out, I need money.

24
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:51,350
I just have to make money first.

25
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:02,590
Ms. Kang, are you still planning
to come in to work today?

26
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:04,030
"Are you still planning to come in?"

27
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:08,330
So stiff.
He is as rigid as a wooden board.

28
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:14,940
Yes, I will be there.

29
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:17,540
(Yes, I will be there.)

30
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:33,360
Tell me,

31
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:36,860
have you ever regretted
taking Da Mi in?

32
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,400
Of course I have, Mother.

33
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:42,400
I suppose so.

34
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:45,000
How could you not feel that way?

35
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:48,040
Dozens of times throughout my life.

36
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,510
I probably should not say this
in front of you,

37
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:55,150
but when their father
walked out like that,

38
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:56,550
I regretted it so much.

39
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,920
I thought,
"I never should have done this."

40
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:21,970
Now she will not even look at me.

41
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:27,880
I truly wanted to provide
a warm and safe shelter...

42
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:29,480
for her whole life.

43
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:34,020
I felt like I broke that promise...

44
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:36,020
and wounded such a young child
all over again.

45
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:38,790
Even now,

46
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:40,830
I feel most guilty
about letting Da Mi down.

47
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:44,030
Still, she grew up well
without turning sour.

48
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:46,800
You should just be
grateful for that.

49
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:51,400
Do not scold her too harshly
for quitting the department store.

50
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,240
And giving Dae Chi
the savings account...

51
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:55,640
you had set aside for Da Mi...

52
00:03:57,010 --> 00:03:58,080
I do not know.

53
00:03:58,610 --> 00:04:00,480
I doubt that was
the right thing to do.

54
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:04,820
Yes.

55
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:08,520
By the way, Mother,
is something bothering you?

56
00:04:09,250 --> 00:04:10,520
No, why do you ask?

57
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:12,520
You just seem that way.

58
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:15,330
Something is going on, is it not?

59
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:17,930
Please tell me.

60
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:20,670
What could you possibly have
that you cannot share with me?

61
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:24,570
You are the one
with a mountain of worries.

62
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:28,140
I told you nothing is wrong.
You are making a fuss over nothing.

63
00:04:30,540 --> 00:04:31,640
I will get breakfast ready.

64
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:43,660
She is far too quick on the uptake.

65
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,520
My goodness.

66
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:51,500
If she finds out they all
moved right into this neighborhood,

67
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:55,170
she will faint from the shock.
What on earth am I going to do?

68
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:08,550
Where is Se Na?

69
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:11,620
Her bed was neatly made,
so I called her.

70
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:14,550
She said she had an errand
and left early this morning.

71
00:05:15,150 --> 00:05:16,220
What kind of errand?

72
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,990
Ms. Se Na said she was busy
and hung up first,

73
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:20,830
so I did not get a chance
to ask, ma'am.

74
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:30,370
Grandma gave her that task lately,
so she has been totally swamped...

75
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:31,670
trying to get it done.

76
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:33,810
She probably went to see the debtor.

77
00:05:40,410 --> 00:05:42,450
By the way, Seung Yun.

78
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:45,120
I meant to ask you earlier,
but it slipped my mind.

79
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,350
All the money you made working
as a designer in the US...

80
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:50,120
are you managing it well yourself?

81
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:53,390
I am curious to know
how you are managing your assets.

82
00:05:53,590 --> 00:05:55,590
He is right, Seung Yun.
Rather than handling it alone...

83
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:58,500
or leaving it with strangers,
it would be much safer...

84
00:05:58,630 --> 00:05:59,700
to trust your uncle's
company with it.

85
00:06:00,230 --> 00:06:02,070
After all, nothing beats family
when it comes...

86
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:03,500
to having a strong
support system, right?

87
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:05,540
Don't you agree, Mother?

88
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:07,640
Of course.

89
00:06:09,170 --> 00:06:12,080
Most definitely.
Until the day we die...

90
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:13,440
and even in the next life,

91
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:16,680
family should be
each other's shield.

92
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:19,220
However,

93
00:06:19,550 --> 00:06:21,950
even people living
under the same roof...

94
00:06:22,290 --> 00:06:24,720
have their own bowls to fill.

95
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,990
As for Seung Yun's money...

96
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:28,790
He is a grown man now.

97
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,860
Let him take care
of his own affairs.

98
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:32,800
Mother.

99
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:35,470
Seung Yun is still quite young,
so I just thought...

100
00:06:35,530 --> 00:06:36,530
I could help him...

101
00:06:37,030 --> 00:06:38,470
Even I am not prying
into his business,

102
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:40,440
so why are you
sticking your noses in?

103
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:42,670
Stay out of it.

104
00:06:45,610 --> 00:06:47,810
Do you hear me, Jin Hee?

105
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,520
Yes, Mother.

106
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:58,790
Seung Yun, how much
did you actually save up?

107
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:00,530
What are you worth?

108
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:05,030
What do you mean, worth?
I blew it all partying, man. Why?

109
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,870
I have to start saving
from scratch now.

110
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:28,650
Why is everyone so quiet today?

111
00:07:29,990 --> 00:07:33,960
It is like we are all practicing
some vow of silence.

112
00:07:38,930 --> 00:07:42,630
Oh, right, Mom.
Could you pick up Su Ah...

113
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:43,940
from kindergarten for me
this afternoon?

114
00:07:44,670 --> 00:07:46,000
I can watch the restaurant
for a bit.

115
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:47,370
Why?

116
00:07:49,410 --> 00:07:51,880
Su Ah said she really wants
her grandma to come get her.

117
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,280
Right, Su Ah?

118
00:07:57,150 --> 00:07:58,880
Please come get me, Grandma.

119
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:01,250
All right, sweetheart.

120
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,760
Da Mi, why are you
barely touching your food?

121
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,160
I'm done eating.

122
00:08:08,830 --> 00:08:10,290
Grandma, I will be
excusing myself first.

123
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:12,930
Why are you leaving so early?

124
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:18,500
- Is something going on?
- I'm starting a new job today.

125
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:22,140
A job?

126
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:24,540
Kkangda, you found
another job already?

127
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:26,840
Seriously. You said
you were burnt out...

128
00:08:26,910 --> 00:08:28,250
and wanted to take a break.

129
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:32,450
Her mom must've
nagged her relentlessly.

130
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,790
Come on, Mother.

131
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:39,560
She quit without saying a word,
so I was just worried.

132
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:44,360
Did you move to a manager position
at another department store?

133
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,100
It is full-time, right?

134
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,130
It's not at a department store.

135
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,770
I'll tell you all about it later.

136
00:08:52,270 --> 00:08:54,340
Wait. Hey, Da Mi.

137
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:58,340
Makes sense.

138
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:01,310
Knowing our little sister,
she probably couldn't sit still...

139
00:09:01,350 --> 00:09:02,450
without making money
for even one day.

140
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:07,350
Just eat, Mom.
She said she'd tell us later.

141
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:12,690
I'm off.

142
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:16,660
Hey, Kang Da Mi.

143
00:09:19,230 --> 00:09:22,230
I told you to move out,
not to go get another job.

144
00:09:23,070 --> 00:09:26,440
I need money so I can get a place
and actually move out.

145
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,540
You must have money saved up.

146
00:09:28,670 --> 00:09:30,610
You've been pinching pennies
your whole life.

147
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:33,480
Even with your mom stressing out
over Dae Chi's debt,

148
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,110
you didn't bat an eye.

149
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:38,280
- Auntie.
- What?

150
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:39,550
Did I say anything that isn't true?

151
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:42,720
No, you didn't.

152
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:49,130
- If you're done, can I go now?
- Well, anyway...

153
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:52,200
You are moving out
on your own, right?

154
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:54,770
Yes.

155
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,300
Don't go telling your mom
I told you to leave.

156
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,540
I don't need her holding it
against me.

157
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:02,640
Besides,

158
00:10:02,710 --> 00:10:05,710
you're only leaving because you know
it's about time, aren't you?

159
00:10:07,850 --> 00:10:08,910
Please go inside.

160
00:10:09,450 --> 00:10:10,450
See you later.

161
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:17,120
Why can't she just give me
a straight answer?

162
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:18,960
Now I feel uneasy.

163
00:10:19,790 --> 00:10:20,790
Gosh.

164
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:26,960
My arm hurts.

165
00:10:27,030 --> 00:10:30,030
Why are you dragging me around
out of nowhere?

166
00:10:30,870 --> 00:10:32,170
The poor kid just found a job
and is heading out,

167
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:33,300
so why did you chase her down...

168
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:35,170
What nasty things
were you whispering to her?

169
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,640
What do you think I did?

170
00:10:36,810 --> 00:10:40,340
- I didn't say much, seriously.
- I'm warning you, Jo Ri Ja.

171
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:44,080
- What?
- If you make our Da Mi cry...

172
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:48,590
ever again,
I'm cutting you off for good.

173
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:50,150
Do you hear me?

174
00:10:50,490 --> 00:10:52,490
Fine, got it.

175
00:10:54,330 --> 00:10:56,130
Aren't you going to
open the restaurant?

176
00:10:56,390 --> 00:10:58,000
I've made myself clear.

177
00:10:58,600 --> 00:10:59,660
Yes, yes.

178
00:11:01,730 --> 00:11:02,730
By the way,

179
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:05,100
don't you think...

180
00:11:05,170 --> 00:11:06,700
your face looks
a bit thinner lately?

181
00:11:07,770 --> 00:11:08,770
Does it?

182
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:10,940
Yes.

183
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,150
Well,

184
00:11:18,550 --> 00:11:21,290
with your three kids taking turns
giving you a hard time,

185
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:23,790
how could you not lose weight?

186
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:33,830
Seriously. Come on.

187
00:11:35,530 --> 00:11:37,330
This is driving me crazy!

188
00:11:46,310 --> 00:11:48,410
If you keep showing up like this,

189
00:11:48,610 --> 00:11:51,220
I could report you
for illegal debt collection.

190
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:53,150
You are the one
who cut off all contact...

191
00:11:53,450 --> 00:11:55,550
and failed to submit
a repayment plan...

192
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:58,460
for the principal
and overdue interest...

193
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:00,090
within the agreed timeframe,
Kang Dae Chi.

194
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:03,930
On top of that,
I heard you were suspended...

195
00:12:03,930 --> 00:12:05,100
from your job...

196
00:12:08,530 --> 00:12:09,530
How did you know that?

197
00:12:12,070 --> 00:12:15,040
I called your office and asked,
and they told me.

198
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:18,340
It seemed like a new hire
slipped up and shared it, though.

199
00:12:18,510 --> 00:12:21,350
You got private information
from a third party?

200
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:24,050
Take that up with your company.

201
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:26,480
What are you going to do, sir?

202
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:30,120
How do you plan to repay
the overdue interest and principal?

203
00:12:30,490 --> 00:12:33,220
I intend to pay it back.
I will definitely pay you.

204
00:12:34,490 --> 00:12:35,490
For now,

205
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:39,330
considering my sincerity,
could you just leave for today?

206
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:41,570
How can intent
and sincerity pay off your debt?

207
00:12:41,570 --> 00:12:42,670
Are you going to steal the money?

208
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:47,940
I will take care of it myself.
So please, just leave, okay?

209
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:50,510
- I will call you.
- From now on...

210
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:53,340
you had better not avoid my calls.

211
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:54,680
Got it?

212
00:12:56,210 --> 00:12:57,250
I said I got it.

213
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:01,350
By the way, what did you do
to get suspended?

214
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:04,050
Breach of trust? Embezzlement?

215
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:07,490
If you end up getting fired,
what are you really going to do?

216
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:11,600
Don't jinx it.
Why on earth would I get fired?

217
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,130
You startled me.

218
00:13:24,010 --> 00:13:25,240
Tell me,

219
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:28,280
have you ever regretted
taking Da Mi in?

220
00:13:28,650 --> 00:13:30,650
Of course I have, Mother.

221
00:13:31,550 --> 00:13:33,220
Dozens of times throughout my life.

222
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:36,020
But when their father
walked out like that,

223
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:38,090
I regretted it so much.

224
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:40,460
I thought,
"I never should have done this."

225
00:13:48,770 --> 00:13:51,300
- Hello.
- Hello. I am here to see...

226
00:13:51,370 --> 00:13:53,440
Head Designer Cha Seung Yun.

227
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:55,410
I was told I should check in...

228
00:13:55,470 --> 00:13:59,440
- at this desk.
- Yes, please leave your ID here.

229
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:05,320
Here you go.

230
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,850
- Thank you.
- You are welcome.

231
00:14:16,390 --> 00:14:17,390
What is with her?

232
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,160
Isn't she the girl from the store?

233
00:14:20,230 --> 00:14:21,830
Why is she showing up
at our company again?

234
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:25,070
Do not tell me Team Leader Cha...

235
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:33,480
Excuse me.

236
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,950
- Manager Kang.
- Yes, ma'am...

237
00:14:37,010 --> 00:14:38,250
What are you doing here again?

238
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,620
I asked why you came
to our company again.

239
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:43,020
Did Team Leader Cha
call you here again...

240
00:14:48,290 --> 00:14:49,290
What was that?

241
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:51,960
Wait, I do not have time for this.

242
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:58,570
What business would that woman
have at our company?

243
00:14:59,570 --> 00:15:00,640
Obviously,

244
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:03,140
Team Leader Cha persuaded her
to work again, and she came.

245
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:04,170
I am sure of it.

246
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:38,810
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

247
00:15:42,810 --> 00:15:44,450
Seung Yun, how much
did you actually save up?

248
00:15:44,450 --> 00:15:45,920
What are you worth?

249
00:15:47,050 --> 00:15:48,750
What do you mean, worth?

250
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,450
I blew it all partying, man. Why?

251
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:53,360
I have to start saving
from scratch now.

252
00:15:54,530 --> 00:15:56,690
Spent it all having fun
and eating out?

253
00:15:59,030 --> 00:16:01,100
Hiding his money already, is he?

254
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:09,770
Who is it? Come in.

255
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,810
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

256
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:20,020
CEO Jeon, I apologize
for bothering you so early.

257
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:21,720
It is urgent.

258
00:16:22,350 --> 00:16:23,350
Urgent?

259
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:26,520
It is Manager Kang, the one
fired from the department store.

260
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:29,530
What about her?
Isn't that settled already?

261
00:16:29,990 --> 00:16:30,990
Well,

262
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,800
I just saw that woman
reporting for work at our company.

263
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,170
What?

264
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,540
What are you talking about?
Reporting for work at our company?

265
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:42,340
- Why?
- Could it be that she accepted...

266
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,680
the offer she supposedly
rejected last time?

267
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:46,140
Do Yun...

268
00:16:46,610 --> 00:16:47,610
Wait.

269
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:51,010
Are you talking about the job
Team Leader Cha recommended her for?

270
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:55,120
Yes. Otherwise,
why would she be badge-swiping...

271
00:16:55,190 --> 00:16:56,650
to come in?

272
00:16:58,220 --> 00:16:59,660
Are you sure you saw her?

273
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,490
Yes, I saw it clearly
with my own eyes.

274
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,030
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

275
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:10,130
Yes, CEO Jeon.

276
00:17:10,330 --> 00:17:11,840
Please tell Team Leader Cha
of Product Planning...

277
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:13,970
to come up right away.

278
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:26,680
(Hwanggeum Apparel
Lead Design Office)

279
00:17:38,330 --> 00:17:40,200
Excuse me.

280
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:49,740
Oh, my gosh.

281
00:17:50,310 --> 00:17:53,110
This place is beyond messy.

282
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,580
He looked so neat and tidy, too.

283
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,650
Right, the smartest ones
make the quickest escape,

284
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,020
just like my sister-in-law said.

285
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,260
Oh, my goodness.

286
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:12,460
You made it?

287
00:18:13,660 --> 00:18:14,670
Yes.

288
00:18:14,970 --> 00:18:16,270
Where are you headed, though?

289
00:18:17,770 --> 00:18:19,370
Nowhere. Why would I be leaving?

290
00:18:19,870 --> 00:18:21,840
Where should I put my bag?

291
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:23,970
Your bag...

292
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:33,820
First, take this.

293
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:38,420
Is this for me? Thank you.

294
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,260
Do you not drink coffee,
by any chance?

295
00:18:42,890 --> 00:18:44,190
How did you know?

296
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:46,030
It was written all over your face,
Kang Da Mi.

297
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:50,200
Right, I am not good with it.
It keeps me from sleeping.

298
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:54,370
I see. Your desk is right over here.

299
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:56,170
For today,
with what I am working on,

300
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:58,240
all you need to do is observe.

301
00:18:58,980 --> 00:18:59,980
Pardon?

302
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,450
I said you just need to watch today.

303
00:19:10,990 --> 00:19:12,590
If you did not call her in,

304
00:19:12,990 --> 00:19:14,190
what business does Manager Kang...

305
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:15,790
have at our company?

306
00:19:17,130 --> 00:19:18,760
Tell me, Team Leader Cha Do Yun.

307
00:19:20,230 --> 00:19:23,870
I asked you why that Manager Kang
showed up at our company.

308
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:28,240
Are you saying that Kang Da Mi
really came to our company today?

309
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:30,340
Are you sure you saw her,
Assistant Manager Kang?

310
00:19:30,510 --> 00:19:34,010
Yes, I saw her clearly.
She was getting into the elevator.

311
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:38,880
What is going on?

312
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:53,360
If she erased her past...

313
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:55,300
Erase it?

314
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,670
She wants to wipe it out?

315
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:02,740
If so, what would she
deal with first?

316
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:06,910
Is that you, Jin Hee?

317
00:20:08,610 --> 00:20:11,180
Jin Sook. Hey, Jeon Jin Sook.

318
00:20:11,450 --> 00:20:13,280
Mother, stepping out for fresh air?

319
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:17,550
- I asked who was on the phone.
- Right.

320
00:20:19,590 --> 00:20:20,860
It was an employee from work.

321
00:20:21,290 --> 00:20:22,390
"Jeon Jin Sook?"

322
00:20:23,730 --> 00:20:26,460
Is Jeon Jin Sook
someone from your company?

323
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:30,270
Yes, Mother.

324
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:33,300
Jeon Jin Sook?

325
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:38,280
Wait a minute.
If it was someone from work,

326
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:42,680
why would they call her that?

327
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:50,290
Could it be...

328
00:20:51,590 --> 00:20:52,590
Right.

329
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:55,360
(Dr. Ju Kyung Ho)

330
00:20:59,030 --> 00:21:00,060
Yes, Chairwoman.

331
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:03,730
I need you to look into a name
for me privately.

332
00:21:04,170 --> 00:21:05,170
Yes.

333
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:09,440
Please go ahead.

334
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,410
The name is...

335
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:14,650
Jeon...

336
00:21:14,780 --> 00:21:16,210
Jin Sook.

337
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,120
(Jeon)

338
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:31,160
Honey, let us go back. Seriously.
Come on, please.

339
00:21:31,230 --> 00:21:33,130
I told you to drive your cab.
Why keep following me?

340
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,200
Why do you keep following me around?

341
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:36,400
Just call them and say...

342
00:21:36,470 --> 00:21:37,530
that due to unavoidable
personal reasons,

343
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,700
you can no longer come to work.

344
00:21:39,070 --> 00:21:40,370
I told you to settle it
over the phone.

345
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:43,210
Why must you insist on showing up
and quitting in person?

346
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:47,940
If you get caught again this time,
you are as good as dead.

347
00:21:48,310 --> 00:21:51,250
How am I supposed to drive
when I am worried sick?

348
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:54,750
Dr. Ju has been so good to me.

349
00:21:54,750 --> 00:21:56,050
I ought to show some courtesy.

350
00:21:56,150 --> 00:21:57,850
Telling him in person
is the right thing to do.

351
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:00,560
Since when did you care
about things like that?

352
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:02,930
Unbelievable.

353
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:05,760
Why is there so much trash...

354
00:22:05,830 --> 00:22:10,600
- strewn about today?
- Did Ri Ja not sweep this morning?

355
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:13,670
I will wait here,

356
00:22:13,970 --> 00:22:15,240
so just say a quick goodbye
and come out.

357
00:22:15,270 --> 00:22:16,470
All right.

358
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:18,810
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

359
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:19,910
Wait.

360
00:22:23,710 --> 00:22:26,450
No matter how much I sweep,

361
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:28,290
- Honey.
- why is it still so dirty?

362
00:22:29,120 --> 00:22:31,960
This is driving me crazy.
No matter how much I clean,

363
00:22:32,060 --> 00:22:34,660
you cannot even tell.

364
00:22:34,730 --> 00:22:36,390
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

365
00:22:36,460 --> 00:22:37,860
One person cleans up,

366
00:22:38,430 --> 00:22:40,400
and someone else just litters.

367
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,030
What is this?

368
00:22:42,730 --> 00:22:45,970
- Are you going or not?
- I am going. I am going, okay?

369
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,000
- Honey, hurry.
- Ji Young, hurry.

370
00:22:48,070 --> 00:22:50,040
I have to tell him I am quitting.

371
00:22:54,750 --> 00:22:55,950
My gosh.

372
00:23:10,330 --> 00:23:12,260
Coming to my house
twice in one day...

373
00:23:12,330 --> 00:23:13,630
is really crossing the line,
do you not think?

374
00:23:13,930 --> 00:23:15,170
You must have forgotten,

375
00:23:15,830 --> 00:23:17,770
but we already met this morning.

376
00:23:17,900 --> 00:23:19,440
You said you would call
by this afternoon,

377
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:21,340
but I did not hear from you at all.

378
00:23:21,970 --> 00:23:22,970
I was passing by...

379
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:24,910
and stopped by
because I was worried about you.

380
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:27,440
If you just contact me on time,

381
00:23:27,510 --> 00:23:30,980
I would not have to
keep coming over, Mr. Kang Dae Chi.

382
00:23:31,250 --> 00:23:33,250
Could you not even wait
three or four hours?

383
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:38,760
I place an enormous value
on punctuality.

384
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:40,760
Besides,

385
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:44,230
as far as waiting goes,
we have already been very patient...

386
00:23:44,290 --> 00:23:47,260
- at Hwanggeum Capital.
- Please.

387
00:23:49,170 --> 00:23:51,870
My mom's restaurant
is right next door.

388
00:23:52,670 --> 00:23:54,000
I do not want anyone in my family...

389
00:23:54,540 --> 00:23:56,570
to see me like this anymore.

390
00:23:57,210 --> 00:24:00,040
Right.
Your mother is doing well, yes?

391
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,180
What kind of restaurant
does she run?

392
00:24:02,550 --> 00:24:04,350
Why do you care about that?

393
00:24:04,650 --> 00:24:05,950
Well,

394
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:08,990
as your account manager,

395
00:24:09,050 --> 00:24:11,790
it is better for me to know
as much about my client as possible.

396
00:24:16,730 --> 00:24:19,160
- Wait, where are you going?
- Someone might see us.

397
00:24:19,230 --> 00:24:20,500
Just follow me, please.

398
00:24:24,700 --> 00:24:25,770
Dae Chi.

399
00:24:25,770 --> 00:24:27,000
Dae Chi, where are you going?

400
00:24:28,670 --> 00:24:30,140
That was definitely Kang Dae Chi.

401
00:24:31,110 --> 00:24:33,410
Who is that woman
he is dragging along?

402
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:02,270
Excuse me, sir.

403
00:25:07,710 --> 00:25:08,750
Excuse me.

404
00:25:12,080 --> 00:25:13,250
Yes? What is it?

405
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:17,650
What can I do to help you?

406
00:25:19,890 --> 00:25:22,690
I thought I told you
to just shadow me today...

407
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:24,230
and then head out.

408
00:25:24,830 --> 00:25:27,330
Still, since I am
getting paid for this,

409
00:25:27,560 --> 00:25:29,870
I feel awkward just standing around.

410
00:25:31,370 --> 00:25:34,300
If you could explain
what I need to do...

411
00:25:34,370 --> 00:25:37,210
or if there is an assistant manual
that outlines...

412
00:25:37,270 --> 00:25:38,540
the responsibilities
I should handle,

413
00:25:38,610 --> 00:25:40,110
I would appreciate it
if you gave it to me.

414
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:43,550
Just sitting still feels like
such a waste of time.

415
00:25:47,620 --> 00:25:49,320
I do not have a manual.

416
00:25:50,690 --> 00:25:53,020
When we went to
the flea market together,

417
00:25:53,290 --> 00:25:55,090
do you remember what I told you?

418
00:25:55,490 --> 00:25:58,160
About looking at the person
before looking at the clothes.

419
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:00,760
Yes, I remember.

420
00:26:02,230 --> 00:26:04,230
You will be working
right by my side...

421
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:07,470
all day long
for a long time from now on.

422
00:26:07,870 --> 00:26:10,740
So spending just one day
observing me closely...

423
00:26:10,740 --> 00:26:13,240
is not a bad investment,
in my opinion.

424
00:26:13,880 --> 00:26:17,010
Well, if you think that
is a waste of time, then...

425
00:26:17,550 --> 00:26:18,650
nothing can be done about it.

426
00:26:22,150 --> 00:26:25,290
Watching is fine for an hour or two.

427
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:29,090
Excuse me, sir?

428
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:33,960
- Yes?
- Could I at least clean up...

429
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,170
around here then?

430
00:26:36,930 --> 00:26:39,500
Please, at least let me do that.

431
00:26:39,740 --> 00:26:42,410
That way, time will actually
pass by faster.

432
00:26:46,340 --> 00:26:47,580
When did it get like this?

433
00:26:48,210 --> 00:26:49,280
Sure, go ahead and do that.

434
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:51,920
Thank you.

435
00:27:07,600 --> 00:27:10,530
He said I could toss these
in the basement,

436
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:12,700
so let's take them down.

437
00:27:16,970 --> 00:27:19,540
- Ms. Kang Da Mi?
- Hello, Team Leader Cha.

438
00:27:43,770 --> 00:27:45,640
(Mission: Mompossible)

439
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:05,520
I spotted this book of plays
on my way into the shop.

440
00:28:05,860 --> 00:28:07,760
Would you like to go see it with me?

441
00:28:08,260 --> 00:28:10,390
- CEO Jeon.
- What is going on?

442
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:11,760
You two already know
each other, don't you?

443
00:28:11,860 --> 00:28:13,700
I would like an explanation.

444
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:15,200
When you abandoned
your wife and kids...

445
00:28:15,370 --> 00:28:16,570
to set up a second family,

446
00:28:16,700 --> 00:28:19,140
did you not know you would end up
in such a pitiful state today?

447
00:28:19,470 --> 00:28:21,810
That "Grandma Go" was
actually that jerk Kang Hak Sung?

448
00:28:23,270 --> 00:28:25,280
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
